00:31:13.378 --> 00:31:14.288
DM: but they are

00:31:17.348 --> 00:31:23.708
DM: so unstable and changeable that even as they grow larger and larger and more powerful, they turn

00:31:25.568 --> 00:31:34.228
DM: into nothing so much as great weather fronts that travel across the land but have no will or purpose behind them.

00:31:34.228 --> 00:31:42.048
DM: Or rather, it is better said, their will and purpose changes from moment to moment such that they can never accomplish anything.

00:31:45.148 --> 00:31:48.168
DM: And eventually they grow so big that they fragment into tiny

00:31:49.728 --> 00:31:51.068
DM: motes of possibility

00:31:52.928 --> 00:31:53.788
DM: that grow.

00:31:54.968 --> 00:31:59.908
DM: Sometimes you will see what look like beasts moving through the landscape

00:32:01.788 --> 00:32:02.388
DM: that are

00:32:05.288 --> 00:32:10.968
DM: several of these filaments grown together, and they will eventually merge and grow into bigger and bigger

00:32:11.988 --> 00:32:14.088
DM: locuses of c- chaos.

00:32:17.268 --> 00:32:19.028
DM: My belief is that this creature

00:32:21.268 --> 00:32:23.748
DM: is what happens when one of these great

00:32:24.768 --> 00:32:25.948
DM: chaos storms

00:32:27.188 --> 00:32:29.748
DM: passes over a locus of stability

00:32:31.468 --> 00:32:34.968
DM: and gains a fixed purpose and ability to control its form.

00:32:40.428 --> 00:32:42.928
Delwath: So hold on. Did, do we need...

00:32:44.388 --> 00:32:46.768
Delwath: The locus of stability itself is what we need, right?

00:32:46.768 --> 00:32:48.008
DM: Yes.

00:32:48.008 --> 00:32:50.468
Unknown: And that's what the runes are written on, you think?

00:32:50.468 --> 00:32:51.067
DM: Yes.

00:32:51.068 --> 00:32:54.228
Delwath: Okay. So we don't actually have to kill the creature.

00:32:54.228 --> 00:32:54.368
DM: No.

00:32:56.988 --> 00:32:57.168
Unknown: Uh,

00:33:00.228 --> 00:33:08.148
Unknown: okay. [laughs] I mean, we might end up having to kill the creature.

00:33:08.148 --> 00:33:09.128
Unknown: But in theory...

00:33:15.257 --> 00:33:15.388
DM: Hmm.

00:33:18.208 --> 00:33:18.508
DM: Okay.

00:33:23.348 --> 00:33:26.168
Kenzo: Kenzo, uh, so th- the, the statue's speaking in our mind, right?

00:33:26.168 --> 00:33:26.288
DM: Yeah.

00:33:27.628 --> 00:33:28.888
Unknown: So it hasn't moved at all even.

00:33:28.888 --> 00:33:30.088
DM: Has not moved at all.

00:33:30.088 --> 00:33:32.108
Seeker: It is solid jade.

00:33:32.168 --> 00:33:36.028
Kenzo: Kenzo will, uh, approach the statue and says, um,

00:33:37.948 --> 00:33:38.228
Unknown: "Uh,

00:33:39.628 --> 00:33:48.068
Kenzo: Rai, I know you don't know me, but, uh, I've carried a piece of your hand with me since I was

00:33:49.268 --> 00:33:52.848
Kenzo: a small child. My parents found a piece of you in the deserts,

00:33:54.108 --> 00:33:57.168
Kenzo: and we have, over these past many years-"

00:33:58.308 --> 00:34:00.588
DM: I have seen you in dreams, yes.

00:34:00.588 --> 00:34:02.928
Unknown: Oh, you have?

00:34:02.928 --> 00:34:04.358
Unknown: That's good to know.

00:34:04.358 --> 00:34:04.408
Unknown: Yeah.

00:34:04.408 --> 00:34:06.208
DM: Some of my dreams, I believe.

00:34:06.208 --> 00:34:06.988
Unknown: What's that?

00:34:06.988 --> 00:34:09.048
DM: Some of my dreams, I believe.

00:34:09.048 --> 00:34:10.248
Unknown: I've seen...

00:34:10.248 --> 00:34:11.568
Unknown: You've seen me in your dreams?

00:34:11.568 --> 00:34:12.868
Unknown: 'Cause I've seen a lot of your dreams.

00:34:15.848 --> 00:34:19.208
DM: I've seen you in those dreams, yes.

00:34:20.268 --> 00:34:23.088
Kenzo: Wow. Didn't know that worked that way.

00:34:23.088 --> 00:34:23.228
Unknown: Hmm.

00:34:24.828 --> 00:34:25.968
Unknown: Well, in any case,

00:34:28.008 --> 00:34:28.568
Unknown: it has been

00:34:30.488 --> 00:34:33.018
Kenzo: quite a lot of effort as we have, uh,

00:34:34.508 --> 00:34:38.968
Kenzo: collected these fragments, and they have been

00:34:40.748 --> 00:34:43.508
Kenzo: a big part of how we've been able to get here.

00:34:44.548 --> 00:34:48.247
Kenzo: As you can imagine, it's not been, uh, straightforward to find you here in Limbo.

00:34:49.408 --> 00:34:55.848
Kenzo: So even if it may not be, uh, as useful as you'd like now, it feels right to give this back to you.

00:34:55.848 --> 00:34:56.148
DM: I,

00:34:57.408 --> 00:34:58.508
DM: I appreciate that.

00:34:59.708 --> 00:35:03.968
Kenzo: And, uh, Kenzo, like, kinda, "Ergy, ergy, ergy," like, unscrews the-

00:35:03.968 --> 00:35:04.987
DM: [laughs]

00:35:04.987 --> 00:35:15.008
Kenzo: [laughs] The, the, the jade hand from, uh, the top of his, uh, staff, and then, you know, goes over and, and, uh, you know, respectfully, uh, and humbly

00:35:15.008 --> 00:35:15.408
Unknown: puts

00:35:16.828 --> 00:35:19.968
Kenzo: the, puts the hand back onto, uh, Rai's stump.

00:35:21.448 --> 00:35:22.868
DM: Sort of fuses there.

00:35:25.188 --> 00:35:26.228
DM: There's a sort of,

00:35:27.748 --> 00:35:30.038
DM: um, brief sort of moment of,

00:35:31.248 --> 00:35:31.428
DM: you know,

00:35:33.008 --> 00:35:35.208
DM: kind of a relaxed sigh in your mind.

00:35:39.428 --> 00:35:45.308
DM: You notice that when you put the hand on that, like, most of the rest of the statue is actually quite worn.

00:35:45.308 --> 00:35:55.408
DM: Like, it's, you know, it's like a sort of ancient statue that's, like, been eroded in places, and it's, like, all the, all the bits other than the hand

00:35:55.408 --> 00:36:00.288
DM: is somewhat eroded and, and weathered.

00:36:02.088 --> 00:36:08.348
DM: And it's not that noticeable, but in contrast to the, like, new hand, it's very clear.

00:36:08.348 --> 00:36:10.968
DM: And you do get a sense, like a, a sense through your mind like,

00:36:12.388 --> 00:36:15.388
DM: you know, this is a nice, this is nice.

00:36:15.388 --> 00:36:15.868
DM: Like, it's,

00:36:18.068 --> 00:36:20.788
DM: you know, the effort of sustaining this for

00:36:23.148 --> 00:36:26.468
DM: 30 years, even if it hasn't been 30 years here, is non-trivial.

00:36:26.468 --> 00:36:26.928
DM: And so

00:36:28.768 --> 00:36:29.728
DM: there is a, like a,

00:36:31.108 --> 00:36:35.408
DM: you know, some relief as you attach the hand, like this helps.

00:36:44.098 --> 00:36:47.818
Delwath: What preparations can we make to go to this place?

00:36:54.838 --> 00:36:55.338
DM: It is...

00:36:59.018 --> 00:37:01.458
DM: I mean, it is not far. I have

00:37:02.898 --> 00:37:07.938
DM: relied on the relic of stability myself to keep this place.

00:37:11.898 --> 00:37:12.518
Unknown: What, um,

00:37:14.178 --> 00:37:16.918
Delwath: is it fixed in form or are we likely to encounter

00:37:18.418 --> 00:37:20.338
Delwath: changes like in the rest of Limbo?

00:37:26.878 --> 00:37:27.458
DM: Well, it is

00:37:29.818 --> 00:37:31.218
DM: within the domain of

00:37:35.338 --> 00:37:35.598
DM: the,

00:37:37.298 --> 00:37:38.558
DM: of the order of this

00:37:39.938 --> 00:37:41.138
DM: relic.

00:37:41.138 --> 00:37:42.438
Unknown: Right.

00:37:42.438 --> 00:37:43.878
Unknown: But does the...

00:37:43.878 --> 00:37:44.378
Unknown: Sorry, what I'm trying to get at-

00:37:44.378 --> 00:37:51.018
DM: Does not mean that it is not, uh, possible for the entity that rules there to change things at whim.

00:37:52.438 --> 00:37:58.158
Delwath: That's what I was trying to get at. Should we anticipate dangers from the entity shifting the ground underneath us?

00:37:58.158 --> 00:38:02.878
DM: I would expect great danger, yes, as I am sure they do not wish to

00:38:04.398 --> 00:38:06.138
DM: sacrifice this relic,

00:38:07.918 --> 00:38:10.008
DM: and especially seem interested in

00:38:13.318 --> 00:38:15.978
DM: bringing Limbo and the material plane closer.

00:38:17.058 --> 00:38:17.758
DM: There have been

00:38:19.138 --> 00:38:21.478
DM: moments when things have shifted and I've had to

00:38:22.638 --> 00:38:23.418
DM: push back,

00:38:25.418 --> 00:38:25.698
DM: and

00:38:27.698 --> 00:38:32.238
DM: some of my charges have been lost over time in those moments when my concentration has

00:38:34.458 --> 00:38:35.598
DM: foundered slightly.

00:38:40.798 --> 00:38:41.798
DM: This is why I,

00:38:43.078 --> 00:38:44.158
DM: when I could, asked

00:38:47.818 --> 00:38:50.998
DM: for help, for I don't know how much longer I can

00:38:52.338 --> 00:38:53.258
DM: sustain this.

00:39:05.718 --> 00:39:07.598
Unknown: So should we take a little, a little break?

00:39:07.598 --> 00:39:09.778
DM: Yeah. This is, I mean, this is a great time if,

00:39:11.978 --> 00:39:12.227
DM: you know-

00:39:12.227 --> 00:39:14.238
Kenzo: Feel like we got a little discussion going on here and, uh-

00:39:14.238 --> 00:39:14.598
DM: Yeah, yeah.

00:39:14.598 --> 00:39:15.118
Unknown: Mm-hmm.

00:39:15.118 --> 00:39:16.798
Unknown: Yeah.

00:39:19.318 --> 00:39:20.758
Unknown: That was a great-

00:39:20.758 --> 00:39:21.778
DM: I was gonna say, yeah

00:39:21.778 --> 00:39:23.458
Seeker: ... session though because one of the...

00:39:23.458 --> 00:39:24.758
Unknown: I just think it was nice to do the recaps. It's like,

00:39:25.898 --> 00:39:29.338
Unknown: it felt like a long session because a lot of things happened.

00:39:29.338 --> 00:39:33.258
Unknown: Yeah. Which is, there was a great pacing to it because we were trying to save as we went.

00:39:33.258 --> 00:39:34.158
Unknown: Yeah, that was awesome.

00:39:36.398 --> 00:39:38.498
Seeker: Uh, the Limbo mechanic is really good.

00:39:38.498 --> 00:39:40.218
Unknown: See, Limbo's the best, man.

00:39:40.218 --> 00:39:42.218
DM: Yeah. Should let, let them win.

00:39:42.218 --> 00:39:46.447
DM: Let Limbo leak into the material plane and just, you know, turn everything into-

